    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe vertical separator for a window in a vertical split is not rendered when:\n\n1. The global status line is enabled (`set laststatus=3`)\n2. Minimum window height is zero (`set winminheight=0`)\n4. The window has a winbar\n5. The window has a single row height\n\nThis is observed when using [folke/edgy.nvim](https://github.com/folke/edgy.nvim) side-panes. See folke/edgy.nvim#38\n\nNotice that the vertical separator for the the `bottom` window is missing:\n\n<img width=\"694\" height=\"573\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12666dcf-5eb1-49ef-92ba-52c4bbd8ee07\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\ncat << EOF > winbar_bug_2.lua\nvim.opt.laststatus = 3\nvim.opt.winminheight = 0\n\nvim.cmd(\"topleft vsplit\")\n\n-- bottom window must have a winbar to repro\nvim.wo.winbar = 'bottom'\n\nvim.cmd(\"aboveleft split\")\n\n-- doesn't matter if top has a winbar or not\nvim.wo.winbar = 'top'\n\n-- resize the top window to push bottom down\nvim.api.nvim_win_set_height(0, 1000)\nEOF\n\nnvim --clean -u winbar_bug_2.lua\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe vertical separator is rendered correctly.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1209+g794886aae7\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, vim 9.2.907\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nFrom source, no modifications, `make nvim`",
